    activity. You are responsible for choosing appropriate sources, instructions, destinations,
    sharing settings, and permissions. Do not include passwords, access tokens, or other secrets in
    clips or public support requests.
  </p>

  <h2>Assistant platforms and connected services</h2>
  <p>
    Gleaner runs through your assistant platform and available tools. Features depend on the
    platform, account permissions, and connected services, and may differ between clients. Those
    providers have their own terms, privacy policies, availability, and any applicable charges. You
    are responsible for those accounts and charges; Gleaner's maintainer does not control those
    services.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy, storage, and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    The distributed Gleaner plugin does not operate its own hosted storage backend or analytics
    service. Your assistant and the tools you use process content and save it to the destination you
    select. See the <a href={privacyUrl}>Gleaner plugin Privacy Policy</a> for details about plugin data
    handling. That policy covers the plugin, not the separate policies of this website or third-party
    providers.
  </p>
  <p>
    Check where content is saved and who can access it. Keep backups of anything important.
    Uninstalling Gleaner, disconnecting a tool, or resetting preferences does not automatically
    delete previously saved content. Manage and delete copies through the service or location where
    they are stored.
  </p>

  <h2>Check generated results</h2>
  <p>
    AI-generated summaries, tags, transcripts, and other outputs may be inaccurate, incomplete, or
    misleading. Check important claims against the original source and confirm that saves succeeded
    before relying on them. Gleaner's output is not a substitute for qualified professional advice.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability and warranties</h2>
  <p>
    Gleaner and its documentation are provided as available, without a promise of uninterrupted
    operation, ongoing support, or fitness for a particular purpose. Features may change or be
    discontinued. The software's warranty disclaimer and limitation of liability are set out in the
